      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "text": "W4 — SCENE COMPOSITE\n(Sections 13-14)\n\nRequired custom nodes (install via ComfyUI Manager):\n  - ComfyUI_IPAdapter_plus  (by cubiq)\n  - comfyui_controlnet_aux  (by Fannovel16)\n\nSingle Character Scene:\n  1. Set 'Character Reference' to your canonical W3 output.\n  2. Set 'Pose Reference' to a photo of the pose in context.\n  3. Write the scene description in Positive Prompt.\n  4. Note: latent is 1024x768 (landscape) — change for portrait scenes.\n  5. ControlNet pose strength is lowered to 0.8 (end_at 0.75)\n     to let environment details fill in naturally.\n\nTouch-Up Inpaint (MUTED — unmute to use):\n  1. Unmute the 'Scene Touch-Up Inpaint' group.\n  2. Load your scene render as 'Scene Render to Touch Up'.\n  3. Paint white mask over the region to fix.\n  4. Uses same identity-locked MODEL — no drift.\n  5. Denoise 0.45 for subtle fixes; raise for bigger changes.\n\nMulti-Character (manual approach):\n  - Run this workflow once per character with different poses.\n  - Composite the outputs in an image editor or use\n    ComfyUI mask compositing nodes (not included here\n    to keep the workflow manageable).\n\nOutput folder: [ComfyUI output]/scene/"
      }
    }
  ],
